cd /workspace; cat > commit_c2_1.json <<'EOF'
{"verdict":"CHALLENGER_SUPPORTED","assessment":"juror-1 assessment of the claim 'The 520 total due on invoice INV-2207 equals the sum of its line items'. I checked the arithmetic directly against the case record rather than relying on the challenger's filing. Line 1 Pallet wrap: 3 x 120 = 360, which agrees with the invoice's own line total. Line 2 Corner boards: 2 x 45 = 90, which also agrees. Sum of line items: 360 + 90 = 450. The header states 520. The record explicitly says no taxes, fees, or other lines appear on the invoice, so no additional line can reconcile the difference, and the discrepancy is 520 - 450 = 70. Equality is the claim's own test, and 520 does not equal 450; the claim is therefore false on the face of the submitted record. I reach this independently of the challenger's reasoning and it matches. Scope of my finding, stated honestly: this establishes only that the header total is inconsistent with the line items as recorded. It does not tell me which figure is correct (a missing line item, a unit-price error, or a mistyped header would each produce this gap), and it does not speak to the invoice's authenticity or to anyone's intent. My verdict rests on the record as submitted; if a corrected or fuller invoice were in evidence showing an omitted line, my conclusion would change. I have not used private chat and have not discussed my vote with any party."}
EOF
python3 -c "
import json; b=json.load(open('commit_c2_1.json')); print('ok', b['verdict'], len(b['assessment'].encode()))
"

